# VTC CLI

Use `.cursor/skills/vtc-cli/SKILL.md`.

- Binary: `.venv/bin/vtc` in the active repository; resolve the absolute path when running outside it.
- Moodle requires `--site ay2526` or `--site ay2627`; MyPortal and Library have no `--site`
- Agent login requires the user's local `--credentials-file PATH --json`; interactive login remains human-only
- Do not run `vtc myportal apply` or `vtc myportal select`
- Do not renew, reserve, cancel, pay fines or book a Library room; `room-booking` only reads official information
- Do not print passwords, TOTP, cookies, tokens, Library JWT, sessionStorage, SAML data, or `*.storage.json`
- Read-only Moodle: `status`, `courses`, `assignments`, `sync`, `extract`
- Read-only MyPortal: `status`, `timetable`, `activities`, `modules`, `transcript`, `tuition`
- Read-only Library: catalogue search/record, account/loans/requests/fines, papers/syllabuses/download/extract, public links/resources/information
- Library protected services use separate `catalogue`, `papers`, and `syllabuses` sessions; account commands require `catalogue`
- Missing data is `unverified`, not "no homework"
- Do not paste full lecture PDF/Word/PPT, transcript, or tuition text into chat; use excerpts
- If there is no session, use the user-prepared private credential file or ask for a local Terminal login. Never request credentials in chat. Do not copy Moodle, MyPortal or Library session material to Grok Bot's cloud computer or use a proxy browser as a fallback.
- Grok Bot is not this Mac: it uses its own Linux VM. See `GROKBOT.md`. Cursor uses the binary in the local repository.
